Hey <%= @user.first_name_or_fallback %>,

<%= @stale_apps.one? ? "This app is" : "These apps are" %> still connected to your Dabble Me account (<%= @user.email %>) and can read and add to your journal, but <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "hasn't" : "haven't" %> been used in over a year:

<% @stale_apps.each do |stale_app| -%>
<% hosts = Admin::OauthApps.redirect_hosts(stale_app.application) -%>
- <%= stale_app.application.name.truncate(60) %><%= " (#{hosts.first(2).join(', ')})" if hosts.any? %>: last used <%= stale_app.last_used_at.strftime("%B %Y") %>, added <%= stale_app.application.created_at.strftime("%B %Y") %>
<% end -%>

If you don't use <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %> anymore, remove <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %> from Connected apps. A removed app loses access right away, and you can connect it again any time:
<%= security_url(anchor: "connected-apps") %>

Still using <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %>? You don't need to do anything.

Thanks,
Dabble Me
